<p>I agree with Roget that the two supplements seem to belong in the article - they are necessary to form a complete story and need to be read in a particular order.</p>
<p>I downvoted, for the reasons I outlined on the forums. The characters are fairly one-dimensional, particularly -1, which is yet another god-like alien intelligence that prefers to communicate in modern English full sentences, with a preference for metaphor and an avuncular tone. And the giant space-monster battle failed to elicit any emotional response from me. As I said, I would have preferred a story about David and Emily exploring emotions and themes relating to legacy, tradition and passing the torch, with -1 as a non-speaking catalyst.</p>

